1: 8, 12.8, 1000, 1250, 125; 2: 4, 6.4, 1000, 1250, 250), DN250 (1: 12.8, 20.48, 1600, 2000, 125; 2: 6.4, 10.24, 1600, 2000, 250), DN300 (1: 20, 32, 2500, 3125, 125; 2: 10, 16, 2500, 3125, 250), DN350 (1&2: 16, 25.6, 4000, 5000, 250), DN400 (1&2: 16, 25.6, 4000, 5000, 250), DN450 (1&2: 25.2, 40.32, 6300, 7875, 250), DN500 (1&2: 25.2, 40.32, 6300, 7875, 250), DN600 (1: 78.75, 126, 6300, 7875, 80; 2: 39.375, 63, 6300, 7875, 160), DN700 (1: 200, 320, 10000, 12500, 50; 2: 100, 160, 10000, 12500, 100), DN750 (1: 200, 320, 10000, 12500, 50; 2: 100, 160, 10000, 12500, 100), DN800 (1: 200, 320, 10000, 12500, 50; 2: 100, 160, 10000, 12500, 100), DN900 (2 only: 158.7, 254, 10000, 12500, 63), DN1000 (2 only: 160, 250, 16000, 20000, 100), DN1050 (2 only: 160, 250, 16000, 20000, 100), DN1100 (2 only: 254, 406.3, 16000, 20000, 63), DN1200 (2 only: 254, 406.3, 16000, 20000, 63), DN1350 (2 only: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40), DN1400 (2 only: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40), DN1500 (2 only: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40), DN1600 (2 only: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40), DN1650 (2 only: 400, 640, 16000, 20000, 40).\n\nBattery rows: DN40 (2), DN50 (2), DN65 (1), DN80 (1), DN100 (1), DN125 (1), DN150 (2), DN200 (2), DN250 (2), DN300 (2), DN350 (1), DN400 (1), DN450 (1), DN500 (1), DN600 (2), DN700 (2), DN750 (2), DN800 (2), DN900 (1), DN1000 (1), DN1050 (1), DN1100 (1), DN1200 (1), DN1350 (1), DN1400 (1), DN1500 (1), DN1600 (1), DN1650 (1).\n\nBattery sizes: 28 sizes (no DN1800). Double: DN40, 50, 150, 200, 250, 300, 600, 700, 750, 800 = 10 double → 20 rows; single: 18 rows. Total 38 rows.\n\nThat's a lot of rows to reproduce. Total 84 rows. That's heavy but it's what \"preserve multi-dim tables\" means. However, given output length constraints, maybe I should be careful. The instruction says matrix_tables preserve multi-dim tables. I think we should include both tables fully. It's long but let's do it.\n\nFor model_level characteristics — should I generate them too? That would duplicate the matrix