   \"type_level\": {\n      \"ratio_q2_q1\": {\"value\": 1.6, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"ratio_q4_q3\": {\"value\": 1.25, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null},\n      \"minimum_ratio_q3_q1\": {\"value\": {\"min\": 40, \"max\": null}, \"unit_symbol\": null, \"unit_id\": null}\n    },\n    \"model_level\": [\n      {\"attribute\": \"permanent_flow_rate_q3\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [...]},\n      {\"attribute\": \"overload_flow_rate_q4\", \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\", \"values\": [...]}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"matrix_tables\": [table7, table8],\n  \"recommendation\": {\"id\": \"R49\", \"edition\": 2013, \"scheme\": \"A\", \"accuracy_classes\": [1, 2]}\n}\n\nWait — should scheme be \"A\"? The certificate number \"R49/2013-A-NL1-20.01\": the \"A\" after year is the OIML certificate scheme (A = certificate without accompanying test report... actually scheme A means certificate issued on basis of type evaluation; B = with test report). Given \"-A-\" appears, scheme \"A\" is right.\n\nRecommendation edition: R49:2013 — edition 2013. The doc references OIML R49-1:2013. Good.\n\nDouble-check numbers with commas in AC table:\n- DN40: Q1 0,08 → 0.08; Q2 0,128 → 0.128. Q3 40, Q4 50, ratio 500. ✓ (0.08 × 1.6 = 0.128 ✓)\n- DN50: 0,126 → 0.126; 0,2016 → 0.2016; 63; 78,75 → 78.75; 500 ✓\n- DN65: 0,2 → 0.2; 0,32 → 0.32; 100; 125; 500 ✓\n- DN80: 0,32 → 0.32; 0,512 → 0.512; 160; 200; 500 ✓\n- DN100: 0,5; 0,8; 250; 312,5 → 312.5; 500 ✓\n- DN125: same as DN100 ✓\n- DN150 c1: 2,52 → 2.52; 4,032 → 4.032; 630; 787,5 → 787.5; 250. c2: 1,26 → 1.26; 2,016 → 2.016; 630; 787.5; 500 ✓\n- DN200 c1: 4; 6,4 → 6.4; 1000; 1250; 250. c2: 2; 3,2 → 3.2; 1000; 1250; 500 ✓\n- DN250 c1: 6,4 → 6.4; 10,24 → 10.24; 1600; 2000; 250. c2: 3,2 → 3.2; 5,12 → 5.12; 1600; 2000; 500 ✓\n- DN300 c1: 10; 16; 2500; 3125; 250. c2: 5; 8; 2500; 3125; 500 ✓\n- DN350: 40; 64; 4000; 5000; 100 ✓\n- DN400: 40; 64; 4000; 5000; 100 ✓\n- DN450: 63; 100,8 → 100.8; 6300; 7875; 100 ✓\n- DN500: same 